<title>USA: Ex-Soviets not seen importing wheat - wheat group.</title>
<headline>Ex-Soviets not seen importing wheat - wheat group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia and other countries formerly part of the Soviet Union are not seen importing wheat any time soon, said the top analyst Wednesday for a major U.S. wheat group.</p>
<p>&quot;The former Soviet Union is no longer a factor in the world wheat market ... it's not a player ... they've got to have money to buy,&quot; said Gregg Doud of the U.S. Wheat Associates at a briefing on the world wheat outlook.</p>
<p>Doud appeared skeptical of recent remarks by Russian Agriculture Minister Viktor Khylstun thast Russia would import up to three million tonnes of wheat next year.</p>
